Adapt Books to Video
Maintainer: winLee1118

This distribution contains a generalized agent workflow and Python helpers.
It excludes production examples, user reference videos, generated media,
private production manifests, and local account or machine configuration.

Attribution: Serge Shima, smixs/visual-skills
https://github.com/smixs/visual-skills
Related high-level visual methods include scene-first description, motivated
camera movement, narrative shot function, and spatial readability. These were
reorganized into this workflow. The attributed material is provided under
CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Further methodological sources and boundaries are recorded in:
adapt-books-to-video/references/source-provenance.md
Their license observations describe historical research, not a representation
that external repositories' current contents have been audited or relicensed.

The public edition removes work-specific narrative examples and reference-video
records, adds host-independent execution guidance and installation support,
and preserves the general production protocols and relevant attribution.
